<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO TO DRAIN 3.594 BLN PESOS.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO TO DRAIN 3.594 BLN PESOS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 3.594 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>    150 million    353 days</p>
<p>    150 million    177 days</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     50 days</p>
<p>    500 million     49 days</p>
<p>    700 million     42 days</p>
<p>    600 million     18 days</p>
<p>    700 million     10 days</p>
<p>    144 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
